IELTS.lesson({"test": 3, "part": 3, "title": "Test 3, Part 3 — the discussion", "candidate": "lama", "script": [{"who": "examiner", "text": "We've been talking about a meal you still remember, and I'd like to discuss with you one or two more general questions related to this.", "ar": "كنّا نتحدّث عن وجبة ما زلتِ تذكرينها، وأودّ أن أناقش معكِ سؤالاً أو سؤالين أعمّ يتعلّقان بهذا.", "shot": "two", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/92e9cf50adffde7b.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "Let's consider food and family.", "ar": "لنتناول الطعام والعائلة.", "shot": "two", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/3b33d242e0159932.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "Do families eat together as often as they used to?", "ar": "هل تأكل العائلات معاً بالقدر نفسه الذي كانت تأكل به سابقاً؟", "shot": "examiner", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/a8a5e5e6ff1cfe65.mp3"}, {"who": "candidate", "text": "Less often, although I'm not sure that means what people think it means. The daily meal has mostly gone, yes. The Friday one matters enormously more now, because it's the only one left, so I don't think the total amount of family has actually fallen. It's just all in one place.", "ar": "أقلّ، مع أنّني لست واثقة أنّ ذلك يعني ما يظنّه الناس. الوجبة اليوميّة اختفت في معظمها، نعم. أمّا وجبة الجمعة فصارت أهمّ بكثير الآن، لأنّها الوحيدة الباقية، فلا أظنّ أنّ مجموع العائلة قد تراجع فعلاً. إنّه فقط صار كلّه في مكان واحد.", "shot": "candidate", "sex": "f", "voice": "piper-en_US-amy-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/18be865f938c9ec0.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "Why is food so important in family traditions?", "ar": "لماذا يحتلّ الطعام هذه الأهمّية في تقاليد العائلة؟", "shot": "examiner", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/843ee29d1582b3bf.mp3"}, {"who": "candidate", "text": "Because eating is the one thing that has to happen anyway. You can skip a holiday, but you can't skip dinner. So anything a family wants to pass on gets attached to the meal, because the meal is guaranteed to come round again. That's why the recipe is never really about the recipe. Nobody needs three people to roll vine leaves. It's a meeting with food in it.", "ar": "لأنّ الأكل هو الشيء الوحيد الذي يجب أن يحدث على أيّ حال. تستطيع أن تتجاوز عيداً، لكنّك لا تستطيع أن تتجاوز العشاء. لذلك فإنّ أيّ شيء تريد العائلة توريثه يُربط بالوجبة، لأنّ الوجبة مضمونة التكرار. لهذا فإنّ الوصفة ليست عن الوصفة أبداً. لا أحد يحتاج ثلاثة أشخاص ليلفّوا ورق العنب. إنّه لقاء فيه طعام.", "shot": "candidate", "sex": "f", "voice": "piper-en_US-amy-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/e066b5d247569592.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "Some people say cooking traditional food takes too much time. Would you agree?", "ar": "يقول بعض الناس إنّ طبخ الطعام التقليدي يستغرق وقتاً طويلاً جداً. هل توافقينهم؟", "shot": "examiner", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/4636cb63decdabf0.mp3"}, {"who": "candidate", "text": "It does take too long, and I'd say that's the function and not a fault. Having said that, I can't pretend the women in my grandmother's generation all chose to. Something can be worth keeping and still have been unfair while it was happening, and I think my generation is allowed to keep the first part of that.", "ar": "نعم يستغرق وقتاً طويلاً جداً، وأقول إنّ هذه هي وظيفته لا عيبه. ومع ذلك، لا أستطيع أن أدّعي أنّ النساء في جيل جدّتي اخترن ذلك كلّهنّ. قد يستحقّ شيء أن يُحفظ ويكون مع ذلك ظالماً حين كان يحدث، وأظنّ أنّ من حقّ جيلي أن يحتفظ بالجزء الأوّل منه.", "shot": "candidate", "sex": "f", "voice": "piper-en_US-amy-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/c7d3cf3e106befed.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "Now let's talk about how eating is changing.", "ar": "والآن لنتحدّث عن كيف يتغيّر الأكل.", "shot": "two", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/f0026f901a426d41.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "How has the way people eat changed in the last twenty years?", "ar": "كيف تغيّرت طريقة أكل الناس في العشرين سنة الماضية؟", "shot": "examiner", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/abaae2dbf1fb3a1b.mp3"}, {"who": "candidate", "text": "I'd say the timing has changed more than the food has, where I live. People eat later, and in shifts, because the day doesn't have the shape it used to have. My grandmother's generation ate at two because two was when everyone was free. Nobody is free at the same time now.", "ar": "أقول إنّ التوقيت تغيّر أكثر مما تغيّر الطعام، حيث أعيش. الناس يأكلون في وقت متأخّر، وعلى دفعات، لأنّ اليوم لم يعد له الشكل الذي كان له. جيل جدّتي كان يأكل في الثانية لأنّ الثانية كانت الوقت الذي يكون فيه الجميع متفرّغين. لا أحد متفرّغ في الوقت نفسه الآن.", "shot": "candidate", "sex": "f", "voice": "piper-en_US-amy-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/66dcd174436f9b10.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "Will traditional dishes still be made in fifty years?", "ar": "هل ستظلّ الأطباق التقليديّة تُصنع بعد خمسين سنة؟", "shot": "examiner", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/ea15b1cc7ed8ef53.mp3"}, {"who": "candidate", "text": "Made, yes. Made at home, I'm less sure. I think they'll go the way bread went. Everybody's grandmother baked, nobody's mother does, and nobody thinks bread has disappeared. It's just made by somebody else now, and something did go when that happened, even if it's hard to say what.", "ar": "تُصنع، نعم. تُصنع في البيت، لست واثقة. أظنّ أنّها ستسلك طريق الخبز. جدّة كلّ واحد كانت تخبز، ولا أمّ أحد تخبز اليوم، ولا أحد يظنّ أنّ الخبز اختفى. إنّه فقط صار يُصنع عند شخص آخر، وشيء ما ضاع حين حدث ذلك، حتى لو كان من الصعب تسميته.", "shot": "candidate", "sex": "f", "voice": "piper-en_US-amy-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/650ec7cf9b716dca.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "Is it a problem that people eat more processed food?", "ar": "هل من مشكلة أنّ الناس يأكلون طعاماً مصنّعاً أكثر؟", "shot": "examiner", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/00d7d58efa1a0147.mp3"}, {"who": "candidate", "text": "It depends whether you mean health or culture, and I think those two arguments get mixed up all the time. The health case is simple enough. The other one is weaker than people assume, because a tin isn't the end of anything, and plenty of what we call traditional was itself a shortcut that somebody's great-grandmother would have disapproved of.", "ar": "هذا يتوقّف على ما إذا كنت تقصد الصحّة أم الثقافة، وأظنّ أنّ هاتين الحجّتين تختلطان دائماً. حجّة الصحّة بسيطة بما يكفي. أمّا الأخرى فأضعف مما يفترض الناس، لأنّ العلبة ليست نهاية أيّ شيء، وكثير مما نسمّيه تقليدياً كان هو نفسه اختصاراً ما كانت جدّة جدّة أحدهم لترضى عنه.", "shot": "candidate", "sex": "f", "voice": "piper-en_US-amy-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/c6b7a5c05b0b8487.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "Thank you. That is the end of the speaking test.", "ar": "شكراً لكِ. بهذا ينتهي اختبار المحادثة.", "shot": "two", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/f502144bdfbbc476.mp3"}], "boxes": [{"q": "Do families eat together as often as they used to?", "topic": "Food and family", "model": "Less often, although I'm not sure that means what people think it means. The daily meal has mostly gone, yes. The Friday one matters enormously more now, because it's the only one left, so I don't think the total amount of family has actually fallen. It's just all in one place.", "modelBand": 8.0, "why": "QUALIFY"}, {"q": "Why is food so important in family traditions?", "topic": "Food and family", "model": "Because eating is the one thing that has to happen anyway. You can skip a holiday, but you can't skip dinner. So anything a family wants to pass on gets attached to the meal, because the meal is guaranteed to come round again. That's why the recipe is never really about the recipe. Nobody needs three people to roll vine leaves. It's a meeting with food in it.", "modelBand": 8.0, "why": "EXEMPLIFY"}, {"q": "Some people say cooking traditional food takes too much time. Would you agree?", "topic": "Food and family", "model": "It does take too long, and I'd say that's the function and not a fault. Having said that, I can't pretend the women in my grandmother's generation all chose to. Something can be worth keeping and still have been unfair while it was happening, and I think my generation is allowed to keep the first part of that.", "modelBand": 8.0, "why": "CONCEDE"}, {"q": "How has the way people eat changed in the last twenty years?", "topic": "How eating is changing", "model": "I'd say the timing has changed more than the food has, where I live. People eat later, and in shifts, because the day doesn't have the shape it used to have. My grandmother's generation ate at two because two was when everyone was free. Nobody is free at the same time now.", "modelBand": 8.0, "why": "CONTRAST"}, {"q": "Will traditional dishes still be made in fifty years?", "topic": "How eating is changing", "model": "Made, yes. Made at home, I'm less sure. I think they'll go the way bread went. Everybody's grandmother baked, nobody's mother does, and nobody thinks bread has disappeared. It's just made by somebody else now, and something did go when that happened, even if it's hard to say what.", "modelBand": 8.0, "why": "SPECULATE"}, {"q": "Is it a problem that people eat more processed food?", "topic": "How eating is changing", "model": "It depends whether you mean health or culture, and I think those two arguments get mixed up all the time. The health case is simple enough. The other one is weaker than people assume, because a tin isn't the end of anything, and plenty of what we call traditional was itself a shortcut that somebody's great-grandmother would have disapproved of.", "modelBand": 8.0, "why": "QUALIFY"}], "voices": {"examiner": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "candidate": "piper-en_US-amy-medium-s119"}});
